# What must not be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the WORKING DIRECTORY, not a git commit, and it does not skip a
# path merely because git is not tracking it. So anything large or confusing that lives
# untracked beside the app has to be named here.
#
# .claude/ holds agent worktrees. One of them measured 591 MB, with its own node_modules,
# its own package.json and its own next.config.ts -- a second, nested Next project inside
# the upload. Two separate problems: the upload size, and a nested config that a build's
# file scanning has no reason to handle gracefully. Neither is worth finding out about
# during a production deploy.
#
# Kept in .vercelignore rather than .gitignore on purpose. This is a statement about what
# gets deployed, and .gitignore is shared with other branches whose owners may have their
# own intentions for these paths. Ignoring a worktree in git as well is defensible and is
# not this file's decision to make.
.claude/

# Local scratch and test output. None of it is served: the app is a fully static export.
test-results/
playwright-report/
